==Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Slavic|ljudъ|lang=hr|people, men}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|h₁lewdʰ-|lang=hr}}.

===Noun===
{{infl|hr|noun|g=m|g2=p|head=ljȗdi}} (singular: {{l|hr|čovjek|čȍvjek}})

# [[people]], [[men]]
#: Dva ''čovjeka'' su išla cestom — ''Two '''men''' walked down the street.''
#: Pet ''ljudi'' je išlo cestom. — ''Five '''people''' walked down the street.''

====Declension====
{{hr-decl-noun|čovjek|ljudi|čovjeka|ljudi|čovjeku|ljudima|čovjeka|ljude|čovječe|ljudi|čovjeku|ljudima|čovjekom|ljudima}}

====Usage notes====
This plural form takes suppletive stem in the singular, as can be seen in the declension table. Old dual forms have been preserved in the counting for 2, 3, 4 (also in 11, 12, 13, 14 etc.) which bind plural form of {{term|čovjeka|lang=hr}}

